  "pd": {
    "basis": "published-pre-1930",
    "detail": "Written 1882 by Quirino Mendoza y Cortes and in wide print in Mexico and the US decades before 1930. Mendoza died in 1957, so the basis is publication date, not author death.",
    "sourceEdition": "Traditional C major setting; verified note-for-note against the ingeb.org traditional-melody MIDI and structurally against A. Sedas, 'Cielito Lindo', O Malho, Rio de Janeiro 1922 (IMSLP 663287)",
    "notes": "Melody and changes only; no lyrics carried in this pass. Encoded in real 3/4 at the QUARTER-NOTE pulse: 3 beats per bar, so each 16-bar section spans beats 0-48. The verse's held sixth degree starts on beat 3 and ties over the barline (the tune's signature anticipation). Both sections cadence UPWARD through 7-2-3 to the mid-register tonic, not down to a low tonic. The single-quarter dominant upbeat that precedes each sung verse is intentionally omitted so sections start on the downbeat; its pitch recurs as the last note of each two-bar verse figure."
  },
